        "title": "Cell Cycle and Division: Growth and Diversity",
        "points": [
          {
            "text": "Cell cycle: G1 (growth) → S (DNA replication) → G2 (growth) → M phase (mitosis + cytokinesis)."
          },
          {
            "text": "Mitosis: prophase → metaphase → anaphase → telophase; maintains chromosome number (2n → 2n)."
          },
          {
            "text": "Cytokinesis: cleavage furrow in animals, cell plate in plants; divides cytoplasm."
          },
          {
            "text": "Meiosis: two divisions; produces 4 haploid gametes (n); reduces chromosome number for sexual reproduction."
          },
          {
            "text": "Crossing over in meiosis I: homologous chromosomes exchange segments, creating genetic variation."
          },
          {
            "text": "Checkpoints (G1/S, G2/M, spindle): monitor DNA damage and correct progression; p53 halts damaged cells."
          },
          {
            "text": "Cancer: mutations in checkpoint proteins (p53, Rb) or oncogenes allow uncontrolled division."
          }
        ],
