        "title": "Worked Example: Hematocrit and Oxygen Delivery",
        "storyContext": "Rohan calculates how oxygen delivery changes with hematocrit.",
        "example": {
          "problem": "Normal person: Hct 45%, Hb 15 g/dL, CO 5 L/min, Hb saturation 97%. Anemic person: Hct 30%, Hb 10 g/dL, CO 5 L/min (compensatory), Hb 97%. Arterial oxygen content = (Hb × 1.34 × Sat) + (0.003 × pO₂). Calculate oxygen delivery (DO₂ = CO × CaO₂).",
          "solution": "Normal: CaO₂ = (15 × 1.34 × 0.97) + (0.003 × 100) = 19.5 + 0.3 = 19.8 mL O₂/100mL blood. DO₂ = 5 L/min × 19.8 = 99 mL O₂/min. Anemic: CaO₂ = (10 × 1.34 × 0.97) + 0.3 = 13 + 0.3 = 13.3. DO₂ = 5 × 13.3 = 66.5 mL/min. Anemia reduces oxygen delivery ~33%."
        },
        "emoji": "🧮",
