        "example": {
          "problem": "Why are transition metals like Fe, Cu colored in solution while main-group metals like NaCl are colorless?",
          "solution": "d-block metals have unfilled d-orbitals. Electrons jump between d-orbitals easily, absorbing visible light (colored). Main-group cations (Na⁺) have full shells; no easy transitions, no color."
        },
        "inSimpleWords": "Transition metals (middle of the table) have unique properties: colors, variable charges, magnetic behavior. This is because their d-orbitals are being filled.",
