          "solution": "(a) Cross-sectional area = π(0.01)² = 3.14 × 10⁻⁴ m². Stress = 5,000 / (3.14 × 10⁻⁴) ≈ 1.59 × 10⁷ Pa = 15.9 MPa. (b) Strain = Stress / E = (1.59 × 10⁷) / (2 × 10¹¹) ≈ 7.95 × 10⁻⁵. (c) Elongation = Strain × Original length = (7.95 × 10⁻⁵) × 2 = 1.59 × 10⁻⁴ m ≈ 0.16 mm. (d) Yes, safe—15.9 MPa << 400 MPa breaking stress. The rod elongates by only 0.16 mm."
