        "example": {
          "problem": "[Co(NH₃)₆]³⁺ vs [CoF₆]³⁻: Which is diamagnetic?",
          "solution": "NH₃ is a strong-field ligand, creating large Δ → low-spin → all electrons paired → diamagnetic. F⁻ is weak-field, creating small Δ → high-spin → unpaired electrons → paramagnetic."
        },
        "inSimpleWords": "Strong ligands force electrons to pair up (low-spin, diamagnetic). Weak ligands allow unpaired electrons (high-spin, paramagnetic).",
