          "solution": "Φ(t) = B A cos(θ(t)) = 2 × 0.01 × cos(10t) = 0.02 cos(10t) Wb. At t=0, Φ = 0.02 Wb (maximum). At t=π/20 s, θ = π/2, so Φ = 0 (field parallel to coil plane). At t=π/10 s, θ = π, so Φ = −0.02 Wb (reversed). The flux oscillates sinusoidally from +0.02 to −0.02 Wb with period T = 2π/ω ≈ 0.628 s."
