          "solution": "1. Prevention: (a) No smoking in buildings—enforce strictly. (b) Inspect electrical wiring and appliances monthly; don't overload outlets. (c) Store chemicals (petrol, gas cylinders) in ventilated rooms away from heat. 2. Detection: (a) Install smoke detectors in corridors, labs, and offices; test monthly. (b) Fire alarm bells in every classroom and hallway. (c) Assign staff to check fire exits daily. 3. Suppression: (a) Place fire extinguishers (Class A for wood/paper, Class B for petrol/oil, Class C for electrical) in kitchens, labs, and corridors. (b) Train teachers in extinguisher use (P-A-S-S: Pull pin, Aim at base, Squeeze, Sweep). (c) Connect water hose to sprinkler system in large rooms; keep clear access. 4. Evacuation: (a) Draw evacuation maps showing exits; practise drills monthly. (b) Designate assembly point outside the school, 100 m away. (c) Account for all students and staff at the assembly point; report to firefighters. Result: Fire detected quickly, suppressed before spreading, and people evacuated safely."
