          "solution": "(1) LAW 1 (INERTIA): Dishes stay at rest even as cloth slides under them (friction on cloth is low, on dishes is high). (2) LAW 2: Catching applies a backward force on the ball (and equal-opposite force on your hand, stopping both). a = F/m. (3) LAW 3: You throw ball backward (action); ball pushes you forward (reaction). Skateboard rolls forward—momentum conservation."
